-- @nonassertable closes a named step to assertion by a request
-- (specs/todo/presumption-assertion/CONTRACT.md §6). It is an annotation of
-- its own, kept by exactprint and re-emitted by the printer; this file checks
-- that it parses, round-trips, and changes nothing a rule works out.

§ `The offence`
    GIVEN `did the act`    IS A BOOLEAN
          `had the intent` IS A BOOLEAN
          `has a defence`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- A nullary step a request may not assert: its truth comes from its derivation.
@nonassertable
`offence made out` MEANS `did the act` AND `had the intent` AND NOT `has a defence`

-- Above the GIVEN of a definition with inputs of its own.
@nonassertable
GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`closed with inputs` MEANS x AND `offence made out`

-- Directly above the name line, below the GIVETH: still above the definition.
GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nonassertable
`closed below giveth` MEANS x OR `offence made out`

-- A @desc whose first word is "nonassertable" is a description, not the mark.
@desc nonassertable in name only
GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`described` MEANS x

#EVAL `offence made out` WITH `did the act` IS TRUE, `had the intent` IS TRUE, `has a defence` IS FALSE
-- A two-clause group, and a mark on the definition after it: the group's range
-- stops at its last clause, so the mark is the next definition's, not a stray
-- inside the group.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`clauses` 0 MEANS 1
`clauses` n MEANS n

@nonassertable
`after the group` MEANS `offence made out`

-- A nullary probe, so the section's inputs can be supplied with WITH.
`probe closed` MEANS `closed with inputs` TRUE

#EVAL `probe closed` WITH `did the act` IS TRUE, `had the intent` IS TRUE, `has a defence` IS TRUE
#EVAL `described` TRUE
#EVAL `clauses` 0
#EVAL `clauses` 7
